' 4+1 Scenarios (+1) - Browse and filter Pokémon (US03)
' Version 1.0 - 2026-10-19 - reflects the current working tree
' Shows how the Logical view (HomeViewModel, PokemonRepository) and the Process view (main-thread
' coroutines, Retrofit) support listing all Pokémon: one network call for the whole list, then search,
' sort and filter run in memory; only the type filter needs another call (cached per type).
' C4 equivalent: c4/dynamic-browse-and-filter.puml.
@startuml scenarios-browse-and-filter
!include ../style.puml

title Scenario - browse and filter Pokémon
autonumber

actor User
participant HomeScreen
participant HomeViewModel
participant PokemonRepository
participant PokeAPI <<external>>
participant "PokeAPI Sprites\n(GitHub raw)" as Sprites <<external>>

User -> HomeScreen : opens the app
HomeScreen -> HomeViewModel : observes pokemons
HomeViewModel -> PokemonRepository : getAllPokemons()
PokemonRepository -> PokeAPI : GET pokemon?limit=100000
PokeAPI --> PokemonRepository : every name + URL
PokemonRepository --> HomeViewModel : List<PokemonSummary>
HomeViewModel --> HomeScreen : pokemons (LiveData)
HomeScreen -> Sprites : loads visible sprites (Coil)

User -> HomeScreen : types a name / picks a sort
HomeScreen -> HomeViewModel : onQueryChange() / onSortChange()
HomeViewModel -> HomeViewModel : filters and sorts in memory
HomeViewModel --> HomeScreen : pokemons

User -> HomeScreen : picks a type in the filter panel
HomeScreen -> HomeViewModel : toggleType(type)
HomeViewModel -> PokemonRepository : getPokemonNamesOfType(type)
opt type not cached yet
    PokemonRepository -> PokeAPI : GET type/{type}
end
PokemonRepository --> HomeViewModel : names of that type
HomeViewModel --> HomeScreen : filtered pokemons (types combine with OR)
@enduml
